61955200,-2.76],[1764547200,32.36],[1767225600,10.09],[1769904000,-19.17],[1772323200,2.14],[1775001600,-1.89],[1777593600,5.94],[1780272000,6.38],[1782864000,41.63],[1785542400,-14.81]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does the Central Government Tax Collections data represent?","answer":"The Central Government Tax Collections data represents the total revenue generated by the Indian central government through various forms of taxation, including income tax, corporate tax, Goods and Services Tax (GST), customs duties, and excise duties."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Central Government Tax Collections data?","answer":"This data is a key indicator of the government's fiscal position and the effectiveness of its tax policy. Tax collections affect government spending, budgetary allocations, and deficit financing.^It reflects the economic activity and performance of different sectors of the economy, consumer demand and spending patterns, as tax collections are closely tied to income levels, corporate profits, and consumer spending.^The level of tax collection is essential for policymakers, economists, and businesses to gauge the overall economic environment and plan fiscal policies accordingly.^Tax collections can impact equity markets, as they influence government spending decisions and economic policies, which in turn can affect corporate earnings and investor sentiment."},{"question":"How to interpret the Central Government Tax Collections data ?","answer":"Higher tax revenues suggest robust economic growth, higher corporate profits, increased consumer spending, and also higher compliance with tax laws, or changes in tax policy (like rate hikes). Conversely, a decline can signal an economic slowdown.^Higher tax collections provide the government with more resources for public spending, investments, and debt management."}],"related":[{"slug":"10-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (10Y)"},{"slug":"1-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (1Y)"},{"slug":"3-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (3Y)"},{"slug":"5-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (5Y)"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-headline","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation- Headline"},{"slug":"crude-oil-price-indian-basket","title":"Crude Oil Price (Indian Basket)"},{"slug":"domestic-institutional-investors-diis-investment-equity","title":"Domestic Institutional Investors (DIIs) Investment - Equity"},{"slug":"foreign-portfolio-investments-fpis-equity","title":"Foreign Portfolio Investments (FPIs) - Equity"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-direct-investment-fdi","title":"Gross Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)"},{"slug":"mutual-fund-aum-equity","title":"Mutual Fund AUM- Equity"},{"slug":"primary-issuances-in-equity-market","title":"Primary Issuances in Equity Market"},{"slug":"repo-rate","title":"Repo Rate"},{"slug":"usd-inr-exchange-rate","title":"USD/INR Exchange Rate"}],"title":"Gross Tax Revenue","description":"India's gross tax revenue stands at ₹ 2,138.7 Billion for Aug 2026. Tax revenue trends relative to nominal GDP show whether the tax base is genuinely widening.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's gross tax revenue stands at ₹ 2,138.7 Billion for Aug 2026. Tax revenue trends relative to nominal GDP show whether the tax base is genuinely widening.","Y-o-Y":"India's gross tax revenue stands at -14.81% for Aug 2026. Tax revenue trends relative to nominal GDP show whether the tax base is genuinely widening."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-08-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-13T15:27:38+00:00"}